(7538443, 1204883, 185755, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by snaffles:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Great capture of a very intriguing-looking spider, I don''t know if they regrow their legs but it looks like that''s what this one is trying to do. The ''Pringles can man'' on the backside is hilarious, it does resemble him.  Definitely fits in the grab-bag that makes up Free Study entries.  I''m afraid, though, that the fact that it''s a spider may have caused some voters to let their own dislike sway their vote.  Still, a very well-seen shot and keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Susan </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Susan,<br/>               As a macro and spider enthusiast that is the love/hate relation I have with spider myself, I understand you perfectly. To add-on, I do not know if the spider got the back design first or ''Pringles'', they have to sort out the IP thingy... <br/>              On a more serious note, really thankful for you comments and insight, I am sure they will be very useful and valuable to me. Will do my best and kept in mind what you said. Thanks once again.<br/> <br/>Your''s Sincerely,<br/> <br/>Amber khim</td>', 'Originally posted by snaffles: Greetings from the Critique Club! Great capture of a very intriguing-looking spider, I don''t know if they regrow their legs but it looks like that''s what this one is trying to do. The ''Pringles can man'' on the backside is hilarious, it does resemble him.  Definitely fits in the grab-bag that makes up Free Study entries.  I''m afraid, though, that the fact that it''s a spider may have caused some voters to let their own dislike sway their vote.  Still, a very well-seen shot and keep up the good work! Susan   Hi Susan,               As a macro and spider enthusiast that is the love/hate relation I have with spider myself, I understand you perfectly. To add-on, I do not know if the spider got the back design first or ''Pringles'', they have to sort out the IP thingy...               On a more serious note, really thankful for you comments and insight, I am sure they will be very useful and valuable to me. Will do my best and kept in mind what you said. Thanks once again. Your''s Sincerely, Amber khim', '2017-10-08 12:28:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7538446, 1204883, 185755, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by streetpigeon:</b></div><hr/><i> Wild looking spider.  What''s that guy from the Pringles can doing on its abdomen?  Product placement, I guess. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi, thanks for the comments. It''s really a cute spider. The "Pringles can" face on it''s abdomen resembles a human face to scare away predator, I guess.</td>', 'Originally posted by streetpigeon: Wild looking spider.  What''s that guy from the Pringles can doing on its abdomen?  Product placement, I guess.   Hi, thanks for the comments. It''s really a cute spider. The "Pringles can" face on it''s abdomen resembles a human face to scare away predator, I guess.', '2017-10-08 12:42:13.000000', NULL, 0),
